# local env files — never commit secrets.
#
# `.env*`, not a hand-listed few. The named patterns missed every variant that
# actually exists in this working tree — .env.india (a Meta CAPI token and a
# Razorpay webhook secret), .env_uk_paid (a LIVE Stripe key), .env.final — all
# of which sat untracked and one `git add -A` from being in the history
# permanently. Verified never committed; the pattern is widened so it stays
# that way.
.env*
# the dotless typo. Next.js does not load it, so it is easy to create by
# mistake and not notice — and the patterns above do not catch it.
env.local
env*.local
.env.example

